# Printer dispatch kill switch (Sep 2026)

Dev-only toggle on Packet Manager pauses **dispatch only**. Do not change
Packets Needed eligibility, Resend via FedEx, tracking, or MID save when
this is off.

## Setting

- `crm_settings.fedex_print_batch_enabled` — must be exactly `"true"` to send
- Missing or `"false"` = paused (fail-safe)
- Write: existing Dev `crm_settings` RLS (`role = 'dev'`)
- UI toggle: Packet Manager `isDev` (dev account email) only

## When paused

- Cron `GET /api/postlogic/send-batch` returns HTTP 200 (`skipped`) — Vercel stays green
- Do **not** call PostLogic or `callPdfGeneratorApi`
- Staff/Dev POST send-batch and `/api/packets/manual-send` return 403
- Banner stays the same mint layout; countdown slot shows **Printer / Dispatch Off** for **every** Packet Manager role
- Needed queue still fills

## Window log

`fedex_print_batch_runs` records `skipped` | `sent` | `empty` per Pacific
`batch_id`. A later skip must not overwrite `sent` the same day. Do not
surface this as a Batch windows list on the page.

## MID extras

Dev **Add MID** is a button next to Export List (modal). Same
`packet_mid_extra_options` upsert — no dashed editor row on Needed.
